oh my gosh  in a tournament marked by poor  attendance and middling public interest  cameroon's knockout match against  minnows comoros was exactly what the  organizers were looking for  but scenes of pandemonium at cameroon's  biggest venue have shocked fans and  non-fans alike  witnesses say thousands of supporters  were directed to a gate on the southern  side of olembe stadium  some tried to push their way through  and hundreds were caught and crushed in  the middle  the authorities say eight people have  been killed one of whom was a child and  38 others were injured images emerged on  social media of supporters lying  motionless on the ground  just now there were 50 people i saw  nearly 50 people on the ground the  barriers were shut and people were  pushing they were falling on top of each  other and there were babies in there  with a mixture of grief and disbelief  relatives of the dead and injured  gathered at hospitals in the capitol  this woman questioning how such a thing  could possibly happen  the cameroonian president has asked  people to exercise self-discipline  during the tournament while the  organizers have promised an inquiry  in recent days officials have been  offering free tickets and transport as  they try to fill the stadia but  spectators are still subject to covid  related rules and the cues and delays  along with impatient crowds have proven  a volatile mix  john sparks sky news
 

